# Ionic Framework Rules

## Love INC–specific: client / volunteer onboarding (READ BEFORE DEBUGGING)
- **Not a universal nonprofit rule.** This app intentionally treats **Get Help** (`get-help`) and **Volunteer** (`volunteer`) as **mutually exclusive** in onboarding and gates volunteer **signup** UI (card icons, action sheet, some detail buttons) for users on the **client** path.
- If volunteer actions “don’t appear” or the volunteer sheet “does nothing” for a **Get Help** user, that is often **by design**, not a broken build.
- **Full reference:** `LoveINC/docs/ONBOARDING_CLIENT_VOLUNTEER_RULE.md` — update that doc when product rules change. Other forks/projects may remove or replace this behavior.

## Reference Projects (CRITICAL – Check Before Implementing)
- **SuperSimpleWorkout**: `/Users/jeffdenton/Projects/MobileApps/SuperSimpleWorkout`
  - Goal Tracker UI: FAB, date scroller, color picker, weekday picker – COPY from SuperSimpleWorkout, do NOT guess
  - FAB: `add-circle` icon, color #fe4c40, see `tabGroup/tabs.component.html` and `tabGroup/tabs.component.scss`
  - Other components: `exercises/components/date-scroller`, `exercises/components/color-picker`, `exercises/components/weekday-picker`
- **NephoPhone**: `/Users/jeffdenton/Projects/MobileApps/NephoPhone/NephoPhone`
  - SQLite, Capacitor, live reload, database init, app resume – COPY patterns from NephoPhone
  - Database: `src/app/services/database/database-base.service.ts` – checkConnectionsConsistency (no dbNames arg), no connection close on foreground
  - App component: `src/app/app.component.ts` – DB init, platform.resume handling
- Before implementing SQLite, Capacitor, live reload, or database features: READ the reference project first. Do NOT guess or search the web.

## Platform and Data Storage (CRITICAL – Never Forget)
- This project ONLY runs in the iOS/Android simulator or on a physical device. It NEVER runs on web.
- NEVER add a dev proxy, proxy.conf.json, or proxyConfig. The app always calls APIs directly (https://api.grovlink.com, etc.). Do not reintroduce proxy-based routing.
- Do NOT add web-specific code, browser fallbacks, or PWA support for data storage.
- We ONLY use SQLite for relational data storage. Use @capacitor-community/sqlite.
- Do NOT use localStorage, IndexedDB, or any browser storage as a fallback for SQLite.
- When adding new database features, use the GrovLink database (GrovLinkDatabaseService) or create new SQLite databases as needed. Never introduce non-SQLite storage for relational data.
- There will be more database work in this project. Always use SQLite.

## Default Ionic Controls
- DO NOT embellish or add custom styling to default Ionic controls unless explicitly instructed by the user
- Ionic is its own UI framework with well-designed default components
- Use Ionic components out of the box with their default styling
- Only add custom styling when the user specifically requests it
- When working with forms, use standard Ionic form components (ion-item, ion-input, ion-select, etc.) with their default appearance
- Avoid adding custom CSS classes, borders, backgrounds, or padding to Ionic components unless requested

## Examples of what NOT to do:
- Adding custom card styling to form fields
- Adding custom borders or backgrounds to ion-item elements
- Overriding default Ionic component styles without being asked
- Creating custom wrappers around Ionic components when not needed

## Examples of what TO do:
- Use ion-list and ion-item as-is for form layouts
- Use default Ionic button styles
- Use standard Ionic input field styling
- Only modify styling when the user explicitly asks for it

## Ionic Icons
- ALL Ionic icon imports (addIcons and icons from ionicons/icons) MUST be consolidated in app.component.ts
- Do NOT import addIcons or icons from ionicons in pages, components, or any other files
- When adding a new icon to the app: import it in app.component.ts and register it in the initializeIcons() addIcons() call
- Pages and components should only reference icon names in templates (e.g. name="personCircleOutline"); the icons are registered app-wide at startup

## Component and Page SCSS – Keep It Thin
- DO NOT add new styles to component or page SCSS files unless you are intentionally overriding something
- Between the Ionic theme and our custom theme files (src/theme/variables.scss, typography.scss, cards.scss, global.scss), there should be very little need for new component-level styles
- Prefer using global typography, card, and layout patterns; add component SCSS only for explicit overrides or truly component-specific structure that cannot live in theme files

## Avoid Redundant CSS Classes
- DO NOT create custom CSS classes for typography that duplicates global styles
- Use standard HTML elements (h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, p, span) which already have global styling
- Use global utility classes (.app-title, .app-body, .app-body-secondary, .app-caption) instead of creating component-specific typography classes
- For text inside ion-label, use standard elements - ion-label p and ion-label h2/h3 are already styled globally
- Only create custom classes for:
  - Layout/structure (flexbox, grid, positioning)
  - Component-specific visual treatments (borders, backgrounds, shadows)
  - State-based styling (hover, active, disabled)
  - Spacing that can't be handled by global patterns

## Examples of redundant classes to avoid:
- `.description`, `.intro-text`, `.detail-text` - use `p` or `.app-body-secondary`
- `.title`, `.card-title`, `.content-title` - use `h2`, `h3`, or `.app-title`
- `.organization-name`, `.service-name` - use `h3` (already styled globally)
- `.notification-title`, `.notification-message` - use `h2` and `p` (already styled globally)
- `.detail-value`, `.detail-address` - use `span` or `.app-body-secondary`
- `.user-type-description` - use `ion-label p` (already styled globally)

## Examples of what TO do:
- Use `<h2>{{ title }}</h2>` instead of `<h2 class="content-title">{{ title }}</h2>`
- Use `<p class="app-body-secondary">Text</p>` instead of `<p class="intro-text">Text</p>`
- Use `<span class="app-caption">Date</span>` instead of `<span class="notification-date">Date</span>`
- Use `<ion-label><p>Description</p></ion-label>` instead of `<ion-label><p class="user-type-description">Description</p></ion-label>`
